      "writtenOn": "2021-01-11T23:00:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e Why is the DRP duty cycle being set to 40%?\n\u003e It is just set this port with larger chance for sink.\n\u003e \u003e It seems like this would contradict our Try.SRC policy.\n\u003e No, DRP duty is nothing about noise rejection.\n\u003e Try.SRC still works even if DRP duty is 40%.\nThen I think this change should be moved to another CL, if it is needed at all. Looking at the datasheet, it looks like this change would actually increase the chance of becoming SRC and decrease the chance of becoming SNK (SRC duty cycle from ~32% to ~39%).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7205c416814e2bf3dfc87c539317f3742e005d96",
